{"step_index":843,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-24T23:31:51Z","content":"### Explanation of What You See in the Dashboard\n\nThere are two distinct reasons for what appears on the screen in your screenshot:\n\n---\n\n#### 1. Why the Vespers Stichera says \"6 Stichera of the Saint from the Menaion\"\nIn the Menaion calendar for August 24 (see `annual_almanac_royal_doors_2026.json` line 36438), **Hieromartyr Eutyches is classified as `[6 SM]` (Class V — Six-Stichera Menaion Saint / Format 06)**:\n* According to *Dolnytsky Typikon Part II, Case 2b (Format 06: Weekday with Saint on 6)*:\n  $$\\text{At Lord, I Call...} \\implies \\text{All 6 Stichera are sung to the Saint from the Menaion}$$\n* When a weekday saint has simple rank (`[4 SM]` / Format 02), our updated engine dynamically resolves:\n  $$\\text{At Lord, I Call...} \\implies \\text{3 from the Octoechos, and 3 from the Menaion}$$\n\nThe previous bug was that a static hardcoded string bypassed the logic engine. With our root fix, the engine now dynamically computes the exact distribution directly from the logic JSON schemas.\n\n---\n\n#### 2. Why the Browser Output Did Not Update Instantly\nThe local Cantor Dashboard server (`cantor_dashboard/server.py`) runs Python in memory. Python caches imported modules at startup, so code changes to `digest/formatters/` take effect only when the server is restarted or receives the next resolved request.\n\n---\n\n### Verifying the Live Output via Terminal\n\nRunning the engine directly on August 24, 2026 confirms the updated rubrics:\n\n```\n## DAILY VESPERS\n\nNo kathisma is appointed.  \n*At Lord, I Call…* we sing 6 Stichera of the Saint from the Menaion; Glory... Doxastikon of the Saint; Both now: Theotokion from the Horologion or Octoechos.  \nDaily Prokeimenon (Monday of the Octoechos), Tone IV: \"The Lord hears me when I cry out to Him\"  \nStichos: Whenever I called, the God of my justice heard me.\n**At the Aposticha:** We sing 3 daily Aposticha from the Octoechos; Glory, Both now: Aposticha Theotokion.  \n**At the Dismissal Troparia:** Troparion of St. Eutyches; Glory, Both now: Dismissal Theotokion in Tone IV.  \n```\n\nAll 7 cards for August 24, 2026 now evaluate to `PASS` against our 2010 Lviv Dolnytsky Typikon!\n\n---\n### Summary of Work\n* Traced the Stichera distribution logic to the underlying Menaion classification (`[6 SM]` for St. Eutyches = 6 Menaion Stichera per Dolnytsky Part II Case 2b / Format 06).\n* Confirmed that unranked/simple saints dynamically receive the 3 Octoechos + 3 Menaion distribution.\n* Verified that Tone IV is correctly matched in both Vespers and Matins dismissal theotokia.","thinking":"**Analyzing Rank Code Designation**\n\nI've zeroed in on the `\"rank_code\": \"[6 SM]\"` entry in the almanac. It appears this signifies a \"Six-Stichera Menaion\" designation. Comparing with St. Eutyches' assignment of six Stichera on August 24, this seems to be the case, confirming the Menaion is the source of this designation.\n\n\n**Confirming Menaion Integrity**\n\nI've established a concrete link: the engine's \"[6 SM]\" faithfully renders all six Stichera from the Menaion, matching the Dolnytsky Typikon format. The engine's logic proves 100% accurate in this respect. It's not just about the designation, it is also about the distribution. I also confirmed that if there are fewer than 6 Stichera, the engine defaults to a 3/3 split, 3 from Octoechos and 3 from the Menaion. I am investigating the browser/server synchronization issue now.\n\n\n"}
